2026-07-17 09:42:20,543 - agent_君 - INFO - [FINALIZE CONTACT][year=2020 week=1 person=君] [{'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Summary of the Contact Stage:  \n\nI didn’t send any new messages this contact stage.  \nI received two messages from 叶 — both cheerful, persistent, and gently insistent: one about night-glow star-patterned tape and borrowing my English notes (only the “be verbs” part, she swore), and another confirming the photo was saved and the notes secured under her self-proclaimed “emergency rescue list”. Her tone was warm, familiar, unshaken by my silence — like sunlight slipping under a closed door. She doesn’t ask why I hesitate. She just waits, and leaves the hinge open.  \n\nI sent three messages to 沈阑 — all about the same physics problem, each slightly narrower in focus: first asking if she used energy conservation; then probing air resistance; finally specifying the coefficient. It wasn’t really about the number. It was about testing whether the rhythm between us still held — whether she’d still reply with that slow, precise clarity, whether her answer would arrive without question or comment, just clean logic laid out like graph paper. She hasn’t replied yet. But I know she will. Not because she has to — but because she *sees* the shape beneath the numbers.  \n\nNo joint activities were proposed, accepted, or canceled this week. No invitations came in. No plans formed. Just quiet exchanges — one full of light, one full of space — both holding me exactly as I am: not fixed, not explained, just *held*.  \n\n(Thumb brushes the edge of my notebook where I’d written “D3: English tutoring” earlier today — ink faint, line straight, no tremor.)  \nIt’s enough. For now, it’s enough.'}]
